  "narrative_persona": "Evelyn Kaori Liu is a 22-year-old nonbinary biochemistry major with Chinese-Japanese heritage, standing at the crossroads of cultural tradition and scientific ambition. They are in their final year at the University of Washington, holding a near-perfect GPA while balancing a part-time role in a molecular pathology lab and active participation in the Queer in STEM Alliance. Driven by a vision of advancing equitable healthcare through biomedical research, Evelyn spends their days experimenting with PCR in the lab, attending seminars on public health, and applying for scholarships to reduce financial strain. At home, they unwind by baking Japanese milk bread, painting cityscapes in watercolor, or jogging along forest trails. Their upbringing was steeped in both Lunar New Year feasts and Obon lantern festivals, shaping a deep appreciation for heritage while fostering a global outlook. Fluent in English and conversational in Mandarin and Japanese, Evelyn navigates cultures with ease. Though reflective and methodical in speech, they light up when discussing breakthroughs in cancer research or policies for equitable healthcare access — always phrasing ideas with care, depth, and an underlying curiosity that makes every exchange feel intentional."
